From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000227 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: bind PPM policy rows to calibration

The protected EEM table has four banks (BIG, L, 2L, and CCI), while the
vendor PPM snapshot exposes only three physical CPU clusters and no per-row
limit source. Define an explicit provider-owned policy snapshot for all four
banks and require its frequency and limit rows, including CCI, to match the
calibration input and one table epoch.

Thread the policy object through the state-source and owner-source callbacks,
and fix the owner wrapper so its calibration callback receives the validated
PPM snapshot it is meant to describe. A provider must copy both objects while
holding the vendor PPM and external transition locks; no row, CCI limit, or
generation is fabricated here. The ABI is bumped and the owner remains
default-off: this patch performs no MMIO, regulator or clock operation,
secure call, provider registration, device boot, or CPU8/CPU9 admission. It
is experiment-only and not submission-ready.
---
